  "difficulty_reason": "Counted unit: original Theorem 3.9 of the article (source label thm:main, source0.tex lines 662--675): the multiplication formula that expresses the product in the Ext-algebra of a 2-Calabi-Yau Frobenius extriangulated category in terms of the splitting of the extensions into the two parts of the associated lattice, as stated in the paper. It is delivered with the authors' own complete 43-line proof at source0.tex lines 677--719. H2: the proof is a genuine homological computation rather than a qualifying examination exercise: the solver must start from the expansion of the product in the Ext-algebra, decompose the relevant bimodule into the two lattice parts, track the projective-injective summands through the stable category, and reassemble the terms to obtain the refined formula. Reproducing that computation in the extriangulated setting is well beyond ordinary PhD qualifying level.",
